    "  项目简介": "  About the project",
    "open_mahjong_unity是一款基于unity/python-fastapi的麻将平台项目，该项目遵循MIT许可协议、免费、开源、支持PC/安卓/ios三端互通；目标是支持所有麻将规则、并且提供给玩家自定义规则的选项。欢迎加入q群906497522参与讨论、协助和测试。": "open_mahjong_unity is a mahjong platform built with Unity and Python/FastAPI. It is free, open source, and licensed under MIT, with cross-play on PC, Android and iOS. The project aims to support every mahjong ruleset and let players define their own. Join QQ group 906497522 to discuss, contribute and test.",
    "  随机种子": "  Random seeds",
    "在玩家 A 出牌时，若玩家 B、C 可对该出牌进行操作，则 B、C 会提前看到这张出牌；玩家 D 则会延迟一个「鸣牌保护时间」才看到出牌。若在鸣牌保护时间内 B、C 对出牌进行了操作，玩家 D 会立刻看见出牌，并在「第一追赶时间」之后再看见 B、C 其一执行的鸣牌申请或鸣牌。\n\n由于玩家 D 必定延迟一个第一追赶时间才看见 B、C 其一的鸣牌，若 B、C 在吃碰后快速出牌，这张出牌在 D 的视角中会显得「即时」。因此平台在触发鸣牌保护后进行出牌时，会保证至少再经过「第二追赶时间」才播放动画，避免在 D 的视角中出牌紧贴在吃碰之后生效。\n\n当前默认配置：\n鸣牌保护时间：1.3s\n第一追赶时间：0.7s\n第二追赶时间：0.5s": "When player A discards a tile and B or C can call it, B and C see the tile immediately. Player D sees it after the call-protection interval. If B or C acts during that interval, D sees the discard immediately, then sees the call request or call animation after the first catch-up interval.\n\nBecause D sees a call with this delay, a quick discard after chi or pon could otherwise appear instantaneous. After call protection is triggered, the platform therefore waits at least the second catch-up interval before playing the next discard animation, keeping the two actions visually separate.\n\nCurrent defaults:\nCall protection: 1.3s\nFirst catch-up: 0.7s\nSecond catch-up: 0.5s",
    "战术鸣牌的设计来源于雀渣：在其他家申请鸣牌以后，可用更高优先级的操作打断他家更低优先级的操作，以模拟线下刻意「碰断吃」等战术。\n\n示例一：玩家 A 出牌 T，玩家 B 可吃、玩家 C 可碰。此时 C 选择跳过，但 B 点击了吃牌；由于仍存在可执行的更高优先级操作，系统会再次询问 C 是否要碰，以模拟国标线下允许刻意用碰打断别人吃的情形。\n\n示例二：玩家 A 出牌 T，玩家 B 可吃或和牌，玩家 C 可碰。B 选择吃，C 用碰打断了 B 的吃；此时 B 不再能用和去打断 C 的碰。这符合国标不允许玩家在鸣牌发声后更改自己要执行动作的规则。": "Tactical calls were inspired by Quezha. A higher-priority action can interrupt another player's lower-priority call, reproducing deliberate physical-table tactics such as using pon to interrupt chi.\n\nExample 1: A discards T. B can chi and C can pon. C initially passes, but B chooses chi. Since a higher-priority action remains available, the system asks C again whether to pon. This models the deliberate interruption allowed in physical MCR play.\n\nExample 2: A discards T. B can chi or win, and C can pon. B chooses chi, then C interrupts it with pon. B can no longer change that call into a win to override C. This follows the MCR rule that a player may not change their declared action after calling.",
