    "段位与匹配说明": "Ranks & matchmaking",
    "为适配不同人数的游玩规则的匹配机制，平台目前提供以下两种段位设计\n1.对于每日对于超过100局的麻将规则，使用以级段制为主的段位系统\n2.对于每日对局低于100局的麻将规则，使用以elo为主的匹配系统进行对局，待人数提升后，按照elo排名设计级段制段位，并通过elo对玩家的段位进行赋分\n3.对于娱乐、开发中或不需添加段位机制的规则，不开设段位匹配场": "The platform uses two ranking systems to suit the number of players in each ruleset.\n1. Rulesets with more than 100 daily games primarily use Kyu/Dan ranks.\n2. Rulesets with fewer than 100 daily games use Elo matchmaking. When participation grows, a Kyu/Dan system can be designed from Elo rankings, with ranks assigned accordingly.\n3. Casual rulesets, rules still in development, and rulesets that do not need ranks have no ranked queues.",
    "Elo 匹配\n\n各规则独立计分。虹雀可选半庄8局或全庄16局，川麻血战和血流换三张为半庄战（8副）。按加入顺序匹配，满四人立即进入对局。\n初始 R = 1500，分母 2400。虹雀半庄 K=16，全庄 K=32；川麻 K=32。按最终名次比较三个对手，并列算平局。桌均 R 低于 1500 时追加保护，不设个人保底。\n\n青雀使用独立的局均素点算法，详见青雀页面。国标、立直仅结算段位/PT；自定义对局不计分。": "Elo matchmaking\n\nEach ruleset is scored separately. Hongque offers half games of 8 hands or full games of 16; Sichuan Bloody Battle and Blood Flow Exchange Three use half games of 8 deals. Players are matched in arrival order, and play begins when four join.\nStarting R = 1500; divisor = 2400. Hongque K = 16 for half games and 32 for full games; Sichuan K = 32. Final placement is compared against each of the three opponents, with ties scored as draws. A table average below R 1500 adds protection; there is no individual floor.\n\nQingque uses a separate per-hand raw-score algorithm; see its page. MCR and Riichi settle ranks/PT only. Custom games are unranked.",
    "放弃比赛": "Forfeit game",
    "检测到您有一场正在进行的游戏，是否返回游戏?": "You have a game in progress. Return to the table?",
    "刷新房间列表成功": "Room list refreshed",
    "Elo 匹配\n\n青雀、虹雀、川麻血战、血流换三张独立计分。虹雀可选半庄8局或全庄16局，川麻血战和血流换三张为半庄战（8副），青雀为全庄战。按加入顺序匹配，满四人立即进入对局。\n初始 R = 1500，分母 2400。虹雀半庄 K=16，全庄 K=32，两种局制共用虹雀积分；其他 Elo 规则 K=32。按最终名次比较三个对手，并列算平局。桌均 R 低于 1500 时追加保护，不设个人保底。\n\n问号内显示算法。国标、立直仅结算段位/PT；自定义对局不计分。": "Elo matchmaking\n\nQingque, Hongque, Sichuan Bloody Battle and Blood Flow Exchange Three have separate ratings. Hongque offers 8-hand half games or 16-hand full games; both Sichuan modes use 8-deal half games, and Qingque uses full games. Players join in order and begin when four are ready.\nStarting R = 1500; divisor = 2400. Hongque K = 16 for half games and 32 for full games; both formats share one rating. Other Elo rulesets use K = 32. Placement is compared against each opponent, with ties scored as draws. Table averages below R 1500 receive protection, with no individual floor.\n\nThe question-mark button shows the algorithm. MCR and Riichi use ranks/PT only; custom games are unranked.",
